    "turn_text": "Well, two things I would say about that. The first is we've got to recognize what this crisis is all about, and it's about a race to deeply decarbonize the world, and that requires a break from fossil fuels. It requires as quickly as possible transitioning to a future where we may have to use some fossil fuels occasionally to generate some materials to fuel some particular type of heavy equipment, but we got to dramatically reduce it. And anytime we don't have to use fossil fuel, we should not be using fossil fuel. So that's a huge part of it. And the second is we need to recognize that we're running out of time, that if we don't get this done in the next decade or so, it's kind of game",
